<< /AP << /N 28 0 R >> /BS << /S /I /W .5 >> /DA (/Helv 10 Tf .333333 .333333 .333333 rg) /DV (MY DISABILITY AND DAILY LIFE\n\nI have been living with [your primary diagnosis -- for example: fibromyalgia, bipolar disorder type I, multiple sclerosis, spinal cord injury, traumatic brain injury, schizophrenia, autism spectrum disorder, Crohns disease, COPD, lupus, chronic pain syndrome, PTSD, or another condition] since [year]. I was formally diagnosed by [doctor or specialist name and title] at [clinic, hospital, or health centre name], located in [city, Alberta]. I have been under continuous medical care for this condition since [year].\n\nPHYSICAL IMPACTS:\nMy condition affects my body in the following ways on a daily basis: [Choose and complete what applies to you] I cannot stand or walk for more than [X] minutes without [pain / losing balance / needing to rest]. I experience chronic pain rated at an average of [X out of 10] daily. I require [X hours] of rest during the day in addition to nighttime sleep. I have [frequent / occasional / unpredictable] episodes of [describe symptom -- e.g. seizures, severe fatigue crashes, acute pain flares, dissociation, psychosis, bowel urgency] that occur approximately [frequency -- e.g. 3 times per week / daily / without warning]. I rely on [describe any aids or equipment -- e.g. a wheelchair, walker, CPAP machine, insulin pump, ostomy bag, hearing aids, communication device] to manage daily function. I am [able / unable] to drive. I am [able / unable] to prepare my own meals on most days.\n\nCOGNITIVE AND MENTAL HEALTH IMPACTS:\n[If applicable] My condition also affects my ability to think, concentrate, and function mentally. I experience [describe -- e.g. severe cognitive fatigue, memory impairment, difficulty processing information, anxiety that prevents me from leaving my home, depression that makes basic self-care difficult, psychotic episodes that require hospitalization, dissociative episodes, panic attacks]. These symptoms occur [frequency] and last approximately [duration]. I am [currently / not currently] stable on medication. My condition [is / is not] fully controlled by treatment.\n\nMEDICAL TEAM AND TREATMENT:\nMy current medical team includes: [list -- e.g. family doctor Dr. [name], psychiatrist Dr. [name], neurologist Dr. [name], pain specialist Dr. [name], physiotherapist [name]]. I attend medical appointments approximately [X] times per month. I currently take the following medications: [list medications and doses, or describe generally -- e.g. daily medications for pain management, psychiatric medications requiring regular monitoring, injections every [X] weeks, infusion therapy every [X] months]. My condition is [permanent and progressive / permanent and stable / permanent with episodic crises -- choose one].\n\nWHY I CANNOT WORK:\nI am not able to maintain employment -- full-time or part-time -- on a sustained basis for the following reasons: [Describe specifically -- e.g. I cannot commit to a predictable schedule because my condition flares without warning. I cannot be on my feet for any sustained period. I cannot concentrate for more than [X] minutes at a time. I require [X] hours of sleep and rest that prevent standard work hours. My condition requires frequent medical appointments that cannot be scheduled around a workday. My psychiatric condition makes managing the demands of a workplace environment impossible on most days.] The Government of Alberta assessed my disability as substantially and permanently limiting my ability to earn a livelihood. I have been eligible for AISH on this basis since [year]. The ADAP transition to an employment-focused program is not appropriate for my situation because [my condition has not improved / my limitations are permanent / I have already attempted [X] and been unable to sustain it].) /F 4 /FT /Tx /Ff 4096 /MK << /BC [ .733333 .733333 .733333 ] /BG [ 1 1 1 ] >> /MaxLen 100 /P 25 0 R /Rect [ 36 543 576 625 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (on_disability) /TU (Describe your disability and how it affects your daily life:) /Type /Annot /V (MY DISABILITY AND DAILY LIFE\n\nI have been living with [your primary diagnosis -- for example: fibromyalgia, bipolar disorder type I, multiple sclerosis, spinal cord injury, traumatic brain injury, schizophrenia, autism spectrum disorder, Crohns disease, COPD, lupus, chronic pain syndrome, PTSD, or another condition] since [year]. I was formally diagnosed by [doctor or specialist name and title] at [clinic, hospital, or health centre name], located in [city, Alberta]. I have been under continuous medical care for this condition since [year].\n\nPHYSICAL IMPACTS:\nMy condition affects my body in the following ways on a daily basis: [Choose and complete what applies to you] I cannot stand or walk for more than [X] minutes without [pain / losing balance / needing to rest]. I experience chronic pain rated at an average of [X out of 10] daily. I require [X hours] of rest during the day in addition to nighttime sleep. I have [frequent / occasional / unpredictable] episodes of [describe symptom -- e.g. seizures, severe fatigue crashes, acute pain flares, dissociation, psychosis, bowel urgency] that occur approximately [frequency -- e.g. 3 times per week / daily / without warning]. I rely on [describe any aids or equipment -- e.g. a wheelchair, walker, CPAP machine, insulin pump, ostomy bag, hearing aids, communication device] to manage daily function. I am [able / unable] to drive. I am [able / unable] to prepare my own meals on most days.\n\nCOGNITIVE AND MENTAL HEALTH IMPACTS:\n[If applicable] My condition also affects my ability to think, concentrate, and function mentally. I experience [describe -- e.g. severe cognitive fatigue, memory impairment, difficulty processing information, anxiety that prevents me from leaving my home, depression that makes basic self-care difficult, psychotic episodes that require hospitalization, dissociative episodes, panic attacks]. These symptoms occur [frequency] and last approximately [duration]. I am [currently / not currently] stable on medication. My condition [is / is not] fully controlled by treatment.\n\nMEDICAL TEAM AND TREATMENT:\nMy current medical team includes: [list -- e.g. family doctor Dr. [name], psychiatrist Dr. [name], neurologist Dr. [name], pain specialist Dr. [name], physiotherapist [name]]. I attend medical appointments approximately [X] times per month. I currently take the following medications: [list medications and doses, or describe generally -- e.g. daily medications for pain management, psychiatric medications requiring regular monitoring, injections every [X] weeks, infusion therapy every [X] months]. My condition is [permanent and progressive / permanent and stable / permanent with episodic crises -- choose one].\n\nWHY I CANNOT WORK:\nI am not able to maintain employment -- full-time or part-time -- on a sustained basis for the following reasons: [Describe specifically -- e.g. I cannot commit to a predictable schedule because my condition flares without warning. I cannot be on my feet for any sustained period. I cannot concentrate for more than [X] minutes at a time. I require [X] hours of sleep and rest that prevent standard work hours. My condition requires frequent medical appointments that cannot be scheduled around a workday. My psychiatric condition makes managing the demands of a workplace environment impossible on most days.] The Government of Alberta assessed my disability as substantially and permanently limiting my ability to earn a livelihood. I have been eligible for AISH on this basis since [year]. The ADAP transition to an employment-focused program is not appropriate for my situation because [my condition has not improved / my limitations are permanent / I have already attempted [X] and been unable to sustain it].) >>
endobj
8 0 obj
<< /AP << /N 29 0 R >> /BS << /S /I /W .5 >> /DA (/Helv 10 Tf .333333 .333333 .333333 rg) /DV (I currently receive $[your AISH amount, e.g. $1,685 or $1,940]/month through AISH. My fixed monthly expenses are as follows: Rent: $[amount]. Utilities \(heat, electricity, water\): $[amount]. Groceries and food: $[amount]. Prescription medications: $[amount]. Medical supplies \(e.g. CPAP supplies, wound care, continence products\): $[amount]. Transportation to medical appointments: $[amount]. Other essential expenses \(e.g. phone, internet required for medical management, laundry\): $[amount]. Total essential monthly expenses: $[total]. After all essential expenses, I have approximately $[amount] remaining each month. Under ADAP, my monthly income would drop to $1,740 by January 2028. Combined with Alberta clawing back the $200/month Canada Disability Benefit, my effective monthly income would be $1,540 -- a reduction of $[calculate your difference]/month from what I receive today. This reduction would force me to cut [describe: one meal per day / prescription refills / medical supplies / heat in winter]. I have [no savings / approximately $X in savings that would last approximately X months]. I have [no assets / describe any assets]. I do not have family members who are financially able to support me.) /F 4 /FT /Tx /Ff 4096 /MK << /BC [ .733333 .733333 .733333 ] /BG [ 1 1 1 ] >> /MaxLen 100 /P 25 0 R /Rect [ 36 412 576 494 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (on_financial) /TU (Describe your current financial situation and what the ADAP transition means for you:) /Type /Annot /V (I currently receive $[your AISH amount, e.g. $1,685 or $1,940]/month through AISH. My fixed monthly expenses are as follows: Rent: $[amount]. Utilities \(heat, electricity, water\): $[amount]. Groceries and food: $[amount]. Prescription medications: $[amount]. Medical supplies \(e.g. CPAP supplies, wound care, continence products\): $[amount]. Transportation to medical appointments: $[amount]. Other essential expenses \(e.g. phone, internet required for medical management, laundry\): $[amount]. Total essential monthly expenses: $[total]. After all essential expenses, I have approximately $[amount] remaining each month. Under ADAP, my monthly income would drop to $1,740 by January 2028. Combined with Alberta clawing back the $200/month Canada Disability Benefit, my effective monthly income would be $1,540 -- a reduction of $[calculate your difference]/month from what I receive today. This reduction would force me to cut [describe: one meal per day / prescription refills / medical supplies / heat in winter]. I have [no savings / approximately $X in savings that would last approximately X months]. I have [no assets / describe any assets]. I do not have family members who are financially able to support me.) >>
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /AP << /N 30 0 R >> /BS << /S /I /W .5 >> /DA (/Helv 10 Tf .333333 .333333 .333333 rg) /DV (I currently live in [city], Alberta. I have been a resident of Alberta for [X] years. I rent / own [choose one] my current home. My rent / mortgage is $[amount]/month. My home is [describe any accessibility features you rely on: e.g. ground floor / no stairs / roll-in shower / widened doorways / elevator access]. I [do / do not] have a local support network in Alberta. My support network includes: [e.g. family members who provide care / a medical team I have worked with for X years / a specialist I see every X months / community supports I rely on for [describe]]. If I were forced to relocate, I would lose access to [describe: my specialist / my pharmacy / my care worker / my support system]. Re-establishing care in a new province would require [describe: finding a new family doctor in a province with a doctor shortage / re-applying for disability supports / re-qualifying for coverage of my medical supplies / waiting months for new assessments]. I [have / do not have] a vehicle. The cost of relocating -- including first and last months rent, a damage deposit, moving a household, and transport of medical equipment -- would be approximately $[estimate]. I do not have access to these funds. I am effectively financially unable to exercise my Section 6 constitutional right to move, because the ADAP transition has left me without the means to do so.) /F 4 /FT /Tx /Ff 4096 /MK << /BC [ .733333 .733333 .733333 ] /BG [ 1 1 1 ] >> /MaxLen 100 /P 25 0 R /Rect [ 36 281 576 363 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (on_housing) /TU (Describe your current housing and what relocation would mean for you:) /Type /Annot /V (I currently live in [city], Alberta. I have been a resident of Alberta for [X] years. I rent / own [choose one] my current home. My rent / mortgage is $[amount]/month. My home is [describe any accessibility features you rely on: e.g. ground floor / no stairs / roll-in shower / widened doorways / elevator access]. I [do / do not] have a local support network in Alberta. My support network includes: [e.g. family members who provide care / a medical team I have worked with for X years / a specialist I see every X months / community supports I rely on for [describe]]. If I were forced to relocate, I would lose access to [describe: my specialist / my pharmacy / my care worker / my support system]. Re-establishing care in a new province would require [describe: finding a new family doctor in a province with a doctor shortage / re-applying for disability supports / re-qualifying for coverage of my medical supplies / waiting months for new assessments]. I [have / do not have] a vehicle. The cost of relocating -- including first and last months rent, a damage deposit, moving a household, and transport of medical equipment -- would be approximately $[estimate]. I do not have access to these funds. I am effectively financially unable to exercise my Section 6 constitutional right to move, because the ADAP transition has left me without the means to do so.) >>
endobj
